1
00:00:16,310 --> 00:00:17,310
Is class okay?

2
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:20,060
The professor teaches well

3
00:00:21,150 --> 00:00:23,150
Is there any other general education class you’d recommend besides this?

4
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:26,320
Um... Huh? Ah!

5
00:00:26,730 --> 00:00:29,320
I think the counseling went okay

6
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:34,950
After this, do you have a free period (class break)?

7
00:00:35,530 --> 00:00:35,990
Yes

8
00:00:37,540 --> 00:00:38,790
Hmm...

9
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:41,370
What... let’s go to a café...

10
00:00:41,920 --> 00:00:43,080
Want to do our homework together?

11
00:00:44,750 --> 00:00:45,130
Okay

12
00:00:45,710 --> 00:00:46,090
Then

13
00:01:06,360 --> 00:01:07,360
Ah...

14
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:19,250
Still studying?

15
00:01:20,410 --> 00:01:21,750
Oh, you're doing your homework until so late

16
00:01:22,170 --> 00:01:23,420
You’re craving nicotine

17
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:25,500
Stop it, will you

18
00:01:25,960 --> 00:01:26,960
It’s going to rot my lungs

19
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:30,050
What—? I’m not a kid, you know?

20
00:01:31,380 --> 00:01:32,220
Hey, but let’s stop the assignment now and go

21
00:01:32,220 --> 00:01:34,300
grab a drink

22
00:01:35,010 --> 00:01:35,590
Huh?

23
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:39,060
Hey, we haven't even been working on the assignment for an hour yet

24
00:01:40,520 --> 00:01:42,190
I’m already done

25
00:01:42,890 --> 00:01:44,560
This is a piece of cake

26
00:01:45,650 --> 00:01:47,230
Ah... this is really unfair

27
00:01:47,820 --> 00:01:49,440
So you think Yeongjae is different from that?

28
00:01:50,440 --> 00:01:51,530
Oh, what—just with something like this?

29
00:01:52,820 --> 00:01:54,490
Oh, really! You said your place is around here, right?

30
00:01:55,240 --> 00:01:56,200
Can we go out for fun?

31
00:01:57,120 --> 00:01:57,370
Huh?

32
00:01:58,490 --> 00:01:59,120
Now?

33
00:02:00,370 --> 00:02:01,500
The house is dirty

34
00:02:01,910 --> 00:02:02,910
I don’t mind the child’s situation

35
00:02:03,460 --> 00:02:04,500
Let’s go get some drinks

36
00:02:06,790 --> 00:02:07,500
Hmm...

37
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:10,090
How about 치맥 (chimaek)?

38
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:14,300
- This way

39
00:02:16,840 --> 00:02:17,760
Here?

40
00:02:21,520 --> 00:02:23,520
Of course you can’t go without chicken and beer

41
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:27,560
Since you bought the chicken, you have to eat both of the legs

42
00:02:30,070 --> 00:02:32,190
Yeah, you’re really into junk food, huh?

43
00:02:32,400 --> 00:02:33,400
Yeah

44
00:02:35,360 --> 00:02:36,700
You and I really match well

45
00:02:37,070 --> 00:02:38,490
What taste is there to go with tough meat like that?

46
00:02:39,320 --> 00:02:42,040
Because tough meat is actually much more plain and tastes better, though?

47
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:47,500
Oh, do you remember the name of that chicken place that was in front of our school?

48
00:02:48,130 --> 00:02:50,960
Oh, what was that name again...?

49
00:02:53,720 --> 00:02:54,800
Hoseok’s chicken!

50
00:02:55,510 --> 00:02:58,510
Oh yeah, yeah, yeah—Hoseok’s chicken

51
00:02:59,090 --> 00:03:01,430
- Oh, we really used to go there all the time

52
00:03:01,970 --> 00:03:03,310
It was really delicious

53
00:03:03,680 --> 00:03:05,020
I can't forget that taste

54
00:03:05,230 --> 00:03:06,520
That sweet and sticky seasoning

55
00:03:07,940 --> 00:03:09,520
Let’s go there once next time

56
00:03:10,110 --> 00:03:10,480
Okay

57
00:03:12,570 --> 00:03:13,280
Not really

58
00:03:13,440 --> 00:03:15,820
I don’t know, but it kind of seems like they might not be open for business

59
00:03:17,950 --> 00:03:19,030
Is that so?

60
00:03:33,800 --> 00:03:36,800
But why haven’t you contacted me even once?

61
00:03:40,180 --> 00:03:41,720
You even changed your number

62
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:45,560
You can still keep in touch even if you go abroad to study

63
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:51,100
Did I do something that made you angry?

64
00:03:52,520 --> 00:03:54,150
No, it’s not like that

65
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:56,070
Then why did you do that?

66
00:04:00,990 --> 00:04:02,570
My parents are really strict

67
00:04:03,990 --> 00:04:06,000
Just pressuring me to go do an MBA

68
00:04:06,790 --> 00:04:08,710
It wasn’t even something I went for willingly to study abroad

69
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:11,710
I was just feeling a bit overwhelmed

70
00:04:18,470 --> 00:04:20,930
I was wondering—did I do something that upset you?

71
00:04:22,430 --> 00:04:23,550
I was worried about that

72
00:04:50,040 --> 00:04:50,370
Oh!

73
00:04:52,130 --> 00:04:53,750
What? Did you get hurt?

74
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:58,010
Whether it’s in the past or now,

75
00:04:58,010 --> 00:04:59,630
it’s all the same if you get hurt, right? It’s fine—it's just a slight cut

76
00:05:00,930 --> 00:05:03,760
Saying it’s okay is the same now as it was back then

77
00:05:03,760 --> 00:05:04,760
Come here—about the work

78
00:05:08,020 --> 00:05:09,560
You got badly hurt, didn't you?

79
00:05:44,090 --> 00:05:45,010
- When I… (at that time)

80
00:05:47,850 --> 00:05:49,560
If you kissed

81
00:05:50,520 --> 00:05:52,230
What happened?
